  "executive_summary": {
    "verdict": "PROTOCOL_LINEAGE_FULLY_RECONCILED",
    "summary": "Every historical discrepancy across EXP-07 stages is rigorously resolved and classified. No untracked execution drift occurred in the core diagnostic runs (C22-B, C22-D). Changes across iterations were legitimate versioned protocol evolutions (e.g. OPS-01 to OPS-02 dataset expansion, schedule refinement from 50 to 30 epochs, and Candidate F sampler introduction), while apparent discrepancies between report narrative and machine truth were typographical documentation drafting errors (e.g., 'VV/VH' misnomer and truncated 3-element loss weight vector).",
